Resume Codex threads when relaunching a frontend

When a rumpelpod Codex frontend exits but its per-pod app-server remains
available, launch the replacement TUI with `resume --last`. Preserve the
existing fast path for attaching to a live frontend.
Start a new thread only when no Codex state has been reported for the
pod.

Cover recovery with an integration test that exits the first TUI and
verifies the relaunched frontend restores its remote conversation.
